OPNware os-homer: serves the Homer dashboard via its own isolated caddy
instance (the plain caddy package only, not os-caddy-advanced).

Settings — port (default 9443), listen interface (all / LAN IP / localhost)
and a TLS toggle — regenerate the plugin-owned Caddyfile and restart the
instance. TLS uses caddy's internal certificate authority, the admin API is
off, and caddy state lives in its own data directory. Logs appear in the
core Diagnostics viewer.
